---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "PMI Thresholds and Mortgage Payments";
const description =
  "Understand when PMI changes the better payment scenario by comparing monthly cost, removal timing, and the path to lower housing costs. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-22";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-pmi-thresholds"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">PMI thresholds</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>PMI thresholds and mortgage payments</h1>
    <p>
      This page is for the comparison that looks close on principal and interest, but stops looking close once private mortgage
      insurance enters the monthly payment and stays there longer than expected.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-down-payment-impact">Down payment impact</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="PMI timing review, scenario-comparison framing, and routing between down-payment decisions, monthly-payment modeling, and removal strategies."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when PMI is the reason the payment scenario changes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when two down-payment or loan-structure options only separate clearly after PMI is added to the monthly payment.</li>
      <li>If you need the base payment build first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If the broader tradeoff is reserves versus upfront cash, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-down-payment-impact">mortgage payment down payment impact</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Monthly PMI is only half of the decision</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      The comparison goes wrong when buyers focus only on the first payment. PMI duration matters more than the first monthly payment
      if one path removes the charge quickly and the other leaves it in place for years.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to model</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>Starting monthly PMI cost under each scenario.</li>
        <li>How long PMI is likely to stay in place.</li>
        <li>Whether the loan permits automatic removal, borrower-requested removal, or both.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What changes the answer</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>Credit profile and loan program differences.</li>
        <li>Whether you have a faster PMI-removal path through amortization, appreciation, or borrower request.</li>
        <li>Whether the lower-down-payment option preserves cash that you actually need to keep.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The most important scenario comparison</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Compare the larger down payment, monthly extra, or appraisal strategy against the plain "do nothing and wait" path. That is
      usually where the real break in monthly cost and total cost becomes visible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common interpretation mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Assuming PMI drops automatically on every loan type at the same threshold.</li>
      <li>Comparing only the starting payment and ignoring how long the PMI line survives.</li>
      <li>Treating PMI as a small side cost instead of the reason one scenario stops being attractive.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When to move to a different page</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>If you need the full housing-payment composition, move to <a href="/guides/what-is-piti">what is PITI</a>.</li>
      <li>If the question is whether extra payments should be used to accelerate removal, move to <a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a>.</li>
      <li>If the broader tradeoff is cash down versus liquidity, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/when-can-i-remove-private-mortgage-insurance-pmi-from-my-loan-en-202/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          When can I remove private mortgage insurance (PMI) from my loan?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-down-payment-impact">Compare down payment paths</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">Review PMI removal options</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
